From 1efefda9e6facb5c4f31783d5d7d910801020569 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 05:29:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Reset on every probe-less re-park; mark freshness
 only on local creation

262ddb7 re-armed the fresh marker after each carried reset, so the next
probe-less park skipped evidence again and an undelivered foreign episode
(peer parks a new P after the reset) kept its age/count. A carried reset proves
nothing about peers afterwards, so the marker is no longer re-armed: every
probe-less re-park carries an explicit reset.

The marker also came from AFTER INSERT / status-entry triggers on tasks, which
fire for sync-imported rows and raw status writes. It is now set only by the
local `created` event (sync never appends it), including triage creation, and
consumed by the first probe-less park; the old triggers are dropped.

test_repeated_probe_less_park_evidence_is_emitted_once (added by this PR, not
an original acceptance test) encoded the unsafe skip; it is now
test_every_probe_less_repark_carries_a_reset.

Proof: new/changed tests in test_kanban_wake_episode_probeless.py
(every-repark, reset->new foreign P->third park [scheduled, continued],
sync-imported task, raw corridor entry) 5 RED on 262ddb7, GREEN here.
Wake episode/check/triage/sync/create files: 65 files, 849 passed, 0 failed
(--local, retries 0, 4 workers); triage atomic-park cardinality unchanged.
